\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Cumulative QLIKE loss differential relative to the closing-interval OLS on the HAR benchmark. The figure plots $\DOTSB \sum@ \slimits@ _{t' \le t} d_{t'}$, where $d_{t'} = L_{t'}^{\text  {model}} - L_{t'}^{\text  {OLS}}$ is the daily loss differential, as in \citet  {WelchGoyal2008}, for the closing-interval model with the lowest mean QLIKE in each model class, each on the full predictor set: the lasso, XGBoost (fixed hyperparameters, re-estimated daily) and the MinGRU network (ridge-initialized, trained and selected on QLIKE). Values below zero mean that the model has accumulated a smaller loss than the OLS; the final value divided by 866{} equals the difference in mean QLIKE. Losses are computed against actual realized variance. Over the shaded window, 24 February to 30 April 2020, the cumulative differentials change by \ensuremath  {+}1.60{} (lasso), \ensuremath  {+}0.30{} (XGBoost) and \ensuremath  {+}0.78{} (MinGRU); over the full out-of-sample period they end at \ensuremath  {-}3.09, \ensuremath  {-}0.81{} and \ensuremath  {-}0.05.}}{27}{figure.caption.19}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:rh_cumulative}{{1}{27}{Cumulative QLIKE loss differential relative to the closing-interval OLS on the HAR benchmark. The figure plots $\sum _{t' \le t} d_{t'}$, where $d_{t'} = L_{t'}^{\text {model}} - L_{t'}^{\text {OLS}}$ is the daily loss differential, as in \citet {WelchGoyal2008}, for the closing-interval model with the lowest mean QLIKE in each model class, each on the full predictor set: the lasso, XGBoost (fixed hyperparameters, re-estimated daily) and the MinGRU network (ridge-initialized, trained and selected on QLIKE). Values below zero mean that the model has accumulated a smaller loss than the OLS; the final value divided by \rhrDays {} equals the difference in mean QLIKE. Losses are computed against actual realized variance. Over the shaded window, 24 February to 30 April 2020, the cumulative differentials change by \rhrCumLassoWindow {} (lasso), \rhrCumXgbWindow {} (XGBoost) and \rhrCumNnWindow {} (MinGRU); over the full out-of-sample period they end at \rhrCumLassoTotal , \rhrCumXgbTotal {} and \rhrCumNnTotal }{figure.caption.19}{}}
