\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Cumulative returns of the sign strategy. The top panel plots the cumulative return at mid-quotes, $\DOTSB \sum@ \slimits@ _{t' \le t} r_{t'}$, in units of the straddle premium, for the short-straddle benchmark ($q_t \equiv -1$) and for one model of each class on the full predictor set: the closing-interval elastic net, LightGBM (the specification of Table\nobreakspace  {}\ref {tab:rh_econ_control}) and MinGRU, and the pooled intraday elastic net. The bottom panel plots the cumulative gain over the short-straddle benchmark, $\DOTSB \sum@ \slimits@ _{t' \le t} \bigl  (r_{t'} + R_{t'}\bigr  )$; the markers are each model's 10{} days of largest gain, all of them days with $q_t = +1$ and $R_t \ge 2.99$. Over the 866{} trading days of the out-of-sample period the gain is \ensuremath  {+}104.7, \ensuremath  {+}98.1, \ensuremath  {+}81.1{} and \ensuremath  {+}79.3{} premia, in the order above, and without each model's 10{} best days it is \ensuremath  {+}15.6, \ensuremath  {+}2.4, \ensuremath  {-}6.2{} and \ensuremath  {-}6.3. Without their 10{} best days, 102{} of the 112{} forecasts of the model set have a negative gain.}}{31}{figure.caption.22}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:rh_econ_cumpnl}{{2}{31}{Cumulative returns of the sign strategy. The top panel plots the cumulative return at mid-quotes, $\sum _{t' \le t} r_{t'}$, in units of the straddle premium, for the short-straddle benchmark ($q_t \equiv -1$) and for one model of each class on the full predictor set: the closing-interval elastic net, LightGBM (the specification of Table~\ref {tab:rh_econ_control}) and MinGRU, and the pooled intraday elastic net. The bottom panel plots the cumulative gain over the short-straddle benchmark, $\sum _{t' \le t} \bigl (r_{t'} + R_{t'}\bigr )$; the markers are each model's \rheTopDays {} days of largest gain, all of them days with $q_t = +1$ and $R_t \ge \rheTopRMin $. Over the \rheNdays {} trading days of the out-of-sample period the gain is \rheGainEnet , \rheGainLgbm , \rheGainNN {} and \rheGainPoolEnet {} premia, in the order above, and without each model's \rheTopDays {} best days it is \rheGainExEnet , \rheGainExLgbm , \rheGainExNN {} and \rheGainExPoolEnet . Without their \rheTopDays {} best days, \rheTailNeg {} of the \rheModelSetN {} forecasts of the model set have a negative gain}{figure.caption.22}{}}
