\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Mean absolute SHAP rank of the leading predictor groups over time. At refit $k$ (one every 10{} trading days), $r_{k,A}$ is the rank of group $A$ among the 49{} groups by its mean absolute SHAP value on the out-of-sample block $\mathcal  O_k$ (1 = largest; log scale), plotted at the block's first day $t_k$. Thin lines: one point per refit; thick lines: centered rolling median over 11 refits (about 110 trading days). Groups: the six with the lowest mean rank $\bar  r_A$ averaged over the three tree ensembles; Kendall's $W$ is in Table\nobreakspace  {}\ref {tab:rh_fi_summary}.}}{39}{figure.caption.37}\protected@file@percent }
